{"availability":"available","full":"Gabriel-Dalton/air-canada-fix","name":"air-canada-fix","description":"Concept demo of an AI passenger care copilot for Air Canada that cites the policy clause behind every answer.","category":"Design","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-04-25T17:36:29Z","updated":"2026-07-29T22:30:16Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://air-canada-fix.vercel.app","topics":["anthropic-api","aviation","chatbot","nextjs","tailwindcss","typescript"],"demo":"https://air-canada-fix.vercel.app/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T18:23:23.726Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T18:23:23.726Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T18:23:23.726Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T18:23:23.726Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Next.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A grounded, citation-backed AI passenger-care copilot for Air Canada — built as a concept pitch.","One sentence: a single AI assistant that diagnoses passenger rights under Canada's APPR, recovers delayed baggage under the Montreal Convention, optimizes Aeroplan status and redemptions, and generates rebooking scripts — with every claim anchored to a specific policy clause, and a CEO-facing ops dashboard that surfaces the rage-risk conversations in real time.","In 2024, a B.C. tribunal ruled that Air Canada was legally responsible for incorrect bereavement-fare information its customer-service chatbot had given a passenger — the airline subsequently took the bot down. The episode produced a visible, named gap in Air Canada's customer experience and a credibility cost attached to the very idea of an AI assistant."],"features":["Cite-or-refuse — the system prompt requires every factual claim to name a specific clause from the loaded knowledge block. If it can't be cited, the assistant declines to answer and offers a human handoff. The frontend…","Deterministic tools for the dollar amounts — compensation, baggage allowance, and status-path math run through typed tool calls with hand-written formulas. The model decides when to call a tool, not what the tool…","Built-in escalation — the model has a flag-for-handoff tool and is prompted to use it on rage, distress, or knowledge gaps. The Ops view picks it up within seconds."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Gabriel-Dalton/air-canada-fix/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"a6df6176b26f7a0b22d570b46f7bf16334ecee6ce4d6b54c0ddc9bbd5bb4e743","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T18:23:23.865Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T18:23:23.865Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A grounded, citation-backed AI passenger-care copilot for Air Canada — built as a concept pitch.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Gabriel-Dalton/air-canada-fix/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"a6df6176b26f7a0b22d570b46f7bf16334ecee6ce4d6b54c0ddc9bbd5bb4e743","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Gabriel-Dalton/air-canada-fix/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-08T18:23:23.865Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-07-29T22:30:16Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Gabriel-Dalton/air-canada-fix/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-08T18:23:23.866Z","hash":"a6df6176b26f7a0b22d570b46f7bf16334ecee6ce4d6b54c0ddc9bbd5bb4e743","originalBytes":7226,"storedBytes":7226,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["baggage","every","ops","canada","claim","knowledge","status","tool","air","chat","what","appr","calls","compensation","convention","human","montreal","passenger","under","aeroplan","allowance","api","assistant","clause","copilot","dashboard","estimate","model","against","alliance","alternate","app","block","cite-or-refuse","conversations","dollar","drafts","page.tsx","path","pitch","rebooking","recommend","route.ts","routings","run","sdk","see","star","streaming","surfaces","system","tariff","weeks","agent","agents","alongside","analyze","answer","anthropic","any","before","built","call","cancelle